https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NorKPVdIBeY  (Capo 4)

TIP:  Harold and Don wrote this with a half-step key change which really presents some awkward sharped chords so I've increased the change to a full step.  It still introduces the (F#m) and (Bm) but it's still easier than the half-step although it won't match the recording.  Or you can just ignore the key change completely and play the second half of the song with same chords as the first half by moving the capo up one fret at the key change.
              

